                "text": "**Analyzing Block Sequences**\n\nI'm currently focused on analyzing how the horizontal color blocks shift and change their heights. I've begun dissecting the patterns in a sample set. For instance, the first example revealed an interesting reshuffling, like with block heights 3,4,2,3 which became 3,4,2,. I'm seeking the governing rules here, looking for a core algorithm.\n\n\n**Investigating Sequence Reversal**\n\nI'm now zeroing in on a critical observation: the reversal of block sequences. In example 2, the non-zero blocks 1, 9, 7 became 7, 9, 1 in the output, completely reversed. Curious about how this applies to example 1, I need to verify if this behavior always holds and what the trigger is. Is it total area? Position?\n\n\n**Confirming Positional Swaps**\n\nI've made a crucial breakthrough! It appears I was wrong about full reversals. My tests indicate that only the *first and last* blocks swap positions. In Example 1, the input blocks 3, 4, 8, 5 become 5, 4, 8, 3. Even more convincing, in Example 3, 7, 6, 8, 9 becomes 9, 6, 8, 7. It seems the other blocks retain their positions. I'm now verifying this hypothesis across more examples and focusing on the behavior of the middle values. Are their heights retained? What about their row assignments?\n\n\n",
